---
import '@fontsource/instrument-serif/400.css';
import '@fontsource/instrument-serif/400-italic.css';
import '@fontsource/ibm-plex-sans/400.css';
import '@fontsource/ibm-plex-sans/500.css';
import '@fontsource/ibm-plex-sans/600.css';
import '@fontsource/ibm-plex-mono/400.css';
import '@fontsource/ibm-plex-mono/500.css';
import BaseHead from '../../../components/BaseHead.astro';
import Header from '../../../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../../../components/Footer.astro';
import BrewGuide from '../../../components/coffee/BrewGuide.svelte';
import { METHODS, SOURCES, cToF } from '../../../lib/coffee/index.ts';

const title = 'Coffee Ratio Calculator and Brew Guide';
const description = 'Pick your brewer and your mug and get the coffee, water, temperature, grind and every timed pour, then brew along. Ratios for V60, Chemex, French press, AeroPress, cold brew and espresso.';
const ratioText = (m: (typeof METHODS)[number]) => m.id === 'espresso'
  ? `1:${m.ratio.stronger}–1:${m.ratio.lighter} (yield)`
  : `1:${m.ratio.stronger}–1:${m.ratio.lighter}`;
const tempText = (m: (typeof METHODS)[number]) => m.id === 'cold-brew' ? 'cold or room temp'
  : m.id === 'moka' ? 'just boiled' : `${Math.round(cToF(m.tempC.min))}–${Math.round(cToF(m.tempC.max))}°F`;
const timeText = (m: (typeof METHODS)[number]) => m.timeS.min >= 3600
  ? `${m.timeS.min / 3600}–${m.timeS.max / 3600} h`
  : m.timeS.min < 60 ? `${m.timeS.min}–${m.timeS.max} s`
  : `${Math.floor(m.timeS.min / 60)}:${String(m.timeS.min % 60).padStart(2, '0')}${m.timeS.max !== m.timeS.min ? `–${Math.floor(m.timeS.max / 60)}:${String(m.timeS.max % 60).padStart(2, '0')}` : ''}`;
const cited = [...new Set(METHODS.flatMap((m) => m.sourceIds))].map((id) => SOURCES[id]).filter(Boolean);
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<BaseHead title={title} description={description} />
		<script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify({
			'@context': 'https://schema.org',
			'@type': 'WebApplication',
			name: title,
			url: 'https://jayarr.coffee/tools/brew-ratio/',
			description,
			applicationCategory: 'UtilityApplication',
			operatingSystem: 'Any',
			offers: { '@type': 'Offer', price: '0', priceCurrency: 'USD' },
			publisher: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'JayArr Coffee', url: 'https://jayarr.coffee' },
		})}></script>
	</head>
	<body class="cf-page">
		<Header />
		<main>
			<section class="cf-intro">
				<a href="/tools/" class="cf-back">← All tools</a>
				<p class="cf-kicker">Brew Guide</p>
				<h1>Coffee ratio calculator <em>and brew guide</em></h1>
				<p class="cf-lede">Pick your brewer and your mug. You get the coffee, the water, the temperature, the grind and every pour, timed, then you can brew along with it.</p>
			</section>

			<section class="cf-tool" aria-label="Brew Guide">
				<BrewGuide client:load />
				<noscript><p class="cf-noscript">The interactive guide needs JavaScript. The table below gives the starting ratio, temperature, grind and time for every method.</p></noscript>
			</section>

			<article class="cf-body">
				<h2>Coffee-to-water ratios by method</h2>
				<p>A ratio of 1:16 means 16 grams of water for every gram of coffee. Lower numbers make a stronger cup. These are the starting ranges the guide uses, from stronger to lighter.</p>
				<div class="cf-table-wrap">
					<table>
						<thead><tr><th scope="col">Method</th><th scope="col">Ratio</th><th scope="col">Water</th><th scope="col">Grind</th><th scope="col">Time</th></tr></thead>
						<tbody>
							{METHODS.map((m) => (
								<tr><th scope="row">{m.label}</th><td>{ratioText(m)}</td><td>{tempText(m)}</td><td>{m.grindLabel}</td><td>{timeText(m)}</td></tr>
							))}
						</tbody>
					</table>
				</div>
				<p class="cf-note">Espresso is measured differently: the ratio is the liquid in the cup to the dry coffee, so 18 g in and 36 g out is 1:2. Cold brew is brewed as a concentrate at about 1:6 and diluted one to one before serving.</p>

				<h2>Why your cup is smaller than the water you pour</h2>
				<p>The grounds hold on to water. A filter bed keeps roughly two grams of water for every gram of coffee, so 400 g of water through 25 g of coffee leaves about 350 g in the cup. The guide works backwards from the cup you want, which is why a 12 oz mug at 1:16 needs about 25 g of coffee and 405 g of water, not 355 g.</p>

				<h2>Strength and extraction are different things</h2>
				<p>Strength is how concentrated the cup is, measured as total dissolved solids (TDS). Extraction is how much of the coffee's soluble material made it into the water, as a share of the dry grounds. The SCA's March 2019 brewing control chart, which grew out of E. E. Lockhart's work in the 1950s, plots one against the other and uses 1.15–1.45% TDS and 18–22% extraction as its reference range; earlier Golden Cup guidance used 1.15–1.35%. These ranges help compare brews, and your preferred strength can fall outside them.</p>
				<p>The ratio sets strength most directly. Grind, temperature and time mostly set extraction. That's why a cup can be strong and sour (too little extracted) or weak and bitter (too much water through tired, over-extracted grounds). The strength the guide shows is an estimate from typical extraction for each method, not a measurement.</p>

				<h2>If the cup tastes off</h2>
				<p>Sour and thin usually means under-extracted: grind finer or use hotter water. Bitter and dry usually means over-extracted: grind coarser. <a href="/tools/fix-my-coffee/">Fix My Coffee</a> asks a few questions and gives you one change for the next brew, and the <a href="/tools/grind-guide/">Grind Guide</a> shows what each grind should look like.</p>

				<h2>Related guides</h2>
				<ul>
					<li><a href="/blog/coffee-to-water-ratio-guide/">Coffee-to-water ratio guide</a></li>
					<li><a href="/blog/ultimate-pour-over-coffee-guide-and-best-v60-technique/">V60 pour-over technique</a></li>
					<li><a href="/blog/how-to-use-a-french-press-the-most-amazing-coffee-youve-ever-had/">How to use a French press</a></li>
					<li><a href="/blog/cold-brew-concentrate-guide/">Cold brew concentrate: ratios, steep time and dilution</a></li>
					<li><a href="/blog/why-water-matters-more-than-your-coffee-beans/">Why water matters</a></li>
				</ul>

				<h2>Sources</h2>
				<ul class="cf-sources">
					{cited.map((s) => <li>{s.author}, <cite>{s.title}</cite>{s.year ? ` (${s.year})` : ''}{s.where ? `: ${s.where}` : ''}.</li>)}
				</ul>
			</article>
		</main>
		<Footer />
	</body>
</html>

<style is:global>
	.cf-page { background: #f3ede3; }
</style>
<style>
	main { color: #2a1d15; }
	.cf-intro { max-width: 1180px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 120px 24px 22px; }
	.cf-back { font: 500 12px/1 'IBM Plex Mono', monospace; letter-spacing: .12em; text-transform: uppercase; color: #75655a; text-decoration: none; }
	.cf-back:hover { color: #8f5d22; }
	.cf-kicker { font: 500 12px/1 'IBM Plex Mono', monospace; letter-spacing: .14em; text-transform: uppercase; color: #8f5d22; margin: 26px 0 0; }
	h1 { font: 400 clamp(40px, 6vw, 68px)/.98 'Instrument Serif', Georgia, serif; letter-spacing: -.01em; margin: 10px 0 12px; color: #2a1d15; }
	h1 em { font-style: italic; color: #7a4e30; }
	.cf-lede { font: 400 17px/1.5 'IBM Plex Sans', system-ui, sans-serif; color: #5b4a3d; max-width: 58ch; margin: 0; }
	.cf-tool { max-width: 1180px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 8px 24px 40px; }
	.cf-noscript { font-family: 'IBM Plex Sans', sans-serif; }
	.cf-body { max-width: 760px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 24px 24px 72px; font: 400 17px/1.7 'IBM Plex Sans', system-ui, sans-serif; color: #2a1d15; }
	.cf-body h2 { font: 400 34px/1.1 'Instrument Serif', Georgia, serif; margin: 44px 0 12px; letter-spacing: 0; }
	.cf-body a { color: #7a4e30; text-decoration-thickness: 1px; text-underline-offset: 3px; }
	.cf-table-wrap { overflow-x: auto; border: 1px solid #d9cdbd; border-radius: 12px; background: #fbf8f3; }
	table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; font-size: 15px; }
	th, td { text-align: left; padding: 10px 14px; border-bottom: 1px solid #e6dccd; white-space: nowrap; }
	thead th { font: 500 11px/1 'IBM Plex Mono', monospace; letter-spacing: .12em; text-transform: uppercase; color: #75655a; }
	tbody th { font-weight: 600; }
	td { font-family: 'IBM Plex Mono', monospace; font-size: 14px; }
	tr:last-child th, tr:last-child td { border-bottom: 0; }
	.cf-note { font-size: 15px; color: #5b4a3d; }
	.cf-sources { font-size: 14.5px; color: #5b4a3d; }
	@media (max-width: 640px) { .cf-intro { padding: 96px 16px 18px; } .cf-tool { padding: 4px 12px 32px; } .cf-body { padding: 16px 16px 56px; } }
</style>
